|term[naming-community]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss Whoever maintains a designator's binding: a family, a filesystem, a registry, a store.
  |designation naming-community
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-descriptors
    :anchor descriptor-kinds
    :projection paraphrase
    The holder of a designator's meaning — a family, a filesystem, a registry — not the referent's properties.
  |formal
    :notation <latex:C: names \rightharpoonup referents, \; unique \; within \; C>
    :reading A community is a uniqueness scope over its minted names (operationally: a unique constraint enforced at mint time).
  |rel :kind maintains :to @designator :card *
  |invariant
    Collision policing happens at mint time or the community's designators degrade toward descriptions (D8).
  |marker
    Any UNIQUE index, any "name already taken" error, any registry is one at work.
